[
  {
    "file": "README.md",
    "line": 17,
    "summary": "\"Nothing the model can write turns it off\" overstates the bypass protection, and line 37 of the same README contradicts it by calling the hooks 'a seatbelt against drift, not a sandbox'.",
    "failure_scenario": "The guard only parses command text, and the plugin README says a model could forge read records by reading the signing key. A user who trusts line 17 treats the bypass switch as tamper-proof when it is a best-effort guard."
  },
  {
    "file": "README.md",
    "line": 63,
    "summary": "TStack is listed under 'Built on:', but ADR 0005 says 'Nothing more is taken from TStack' and that Matt's skills and the claude.dev posts win over it; nothing in the repo depends on it.",
    "failure_scenario": "Readers come away thinking the plugin is built on TStack. That contradicts the accepted ADR and goes beyond the old README, which only listed it as a reference link."
  },
  {
    "file": "README.md",
    "line": 30,
    "summary": "The Trace gates row is garbled: 'Refuses an edit unless it is on an open issue's `<n>-` branch, a commit without `#<n>`, and a PR without `Closes #<n>`' attaches all three items to 'unless'.",
    "failure_scenario": "Read literally, it says the plugin refuses an edit unless it is 'a commit without #<n>', which is the opposite of the real rule. The row needs to read: refuses edits off an open issue's branch, commits without #<n>, and PRs without Closes #<n>."
  },
  {
    "file": "README.md",
    "line": 12,
    "summary": "The Quick start never mentions that `plugin.json` depends on `mattpocock-skills@claude-plugins-official`, so installing needs the `claude-plugins-official` marketplace to be available.",
    "failure_scenario": "On a setup where the official marketplace isn't added, `/plugin install trace@cc-agents` cannot resolve the dependency, and the 'working install steps' the issue asks for fail with no hint why."
  },
  {
    "file": "README.md",
    "line": 35,
    "summary": "The Guard row describes the switch protection as only 'Bash writes to Claude Code's settings'. It leaves out installed plugins and the `claude plugin` / `claude config` subcommands that the guard (per GLOSSARY.md) also blocks.",
    "failure_scenario": "A reader who wonders why `claude plugin install …` or a `cp` into the plugins directory was refused finds nothing in the table about it. The row also drifts from the glossary's definition of Guard."
  },
  {
    "file": "README.md",
    "line": 30,
    "summary": "The table marks all edit-gate behaviour as 'Traced repos', but the edit tools are refused changes to settings `env`, `disableAllHooks`, `enabledPlugins` and `hooks` everywhere.",
    "failure_scenario": "In a repo that has not opted in, an agent's Edit to `.claude/settings.json` `env` is still refused. The table implies nothing is gated outside traced repos except the guard and the archive block, which line 15 also repeats."
  },
  {
    "file": "README.md",
    "line": 31,
    "summary": "The Forced reads row says 'every active ADR' must be read before an edit, but ADRs with `applies-to:` count only for edits to matching paths. The row also omits the merge, rebase and cherry-pick commands that wait for the reads too.",
    "failure_scenario": "A user writes a scoped ADR, expects it to block every edit, and sees edits outside its glob go through. Or they get surprised when a `git rebase` is refused for unread docs."
  },
  {
    "file": "README.md",
    "line": 15,
    "summary": "The /trace:setup summary lists checks for gh, Matt's skills and the triage labels, but leaves out the docs check (GLOSSARY.md, docs/adr/). It also omits that the opt-in adds an `archive/**` deny rule to `.claude/settings.json`.",
    "failure_scenario": "A user running setup is surprised by the docs report and by the change to their settings file, which the README never mentions."
